(4.2 Sampling Strategy) Tj 0 -12 Td
(Samples were drawn every ninety seconds over a six hour acquisition window.) Tj 0 -12 Td
(The sampler discards the first reading of each window as a settling artefact.) Tj 0 -12 Td
1 0 0 1 320 700 Tm
(Drift correction is applied before the samples are averaged, not afterwards.) Tj 0 -12 Td
(Averaging first would fold the drift into every mean and hide the correction.) Tj 0 -12 Td
ET
endstream
